{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/382430-mystery-plays-in-hunter-the-reckoning-a-problem","id":382430,"title":"Mystery Plays in Hunter: The Reckoning (A problem)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-26T16:35:04-08:00","id":382430,"title":"Mystery Plays in Hunter: The Reckoning (A problem)","content":"I remember that I played Reckoning with some friends when I was younger and I enjoyed my Redeemer character, though when I had to retire him, due to some &quot;canon&quot; that put a kibosh on a part of his backstory, I had to create another one. I decided to make an Innocent because I liked their child-like curiosity and their rogue-like abilities. When I suggested it to my ST, he told me that it would all depend on the Mystery Play. When I asked if I could start as an Innocent, bypassing the MP entirely, he said that I couldn't and showed me in the book that the to-be Imbued HAS to take part in a Mystery Play. Resigned, I tried to act like what I thought an Innocent would act like. Instead of the Innocent Creed, my character attained the Hermit Creed. I was not pleased.<br /> <br /> The fact that the Mystery Play has to happen tells me that I have less creative control over character creation and the fate of my character's awakening is in the hands of the ST, who may have different ideas on which path my character must travel. This has to stop. I would like it if the Mystery Play is considered optional, only used for players who are indecisive about which Creed to take. Attaching the Mystery Play to my hip didn't ruin the game for me, but it did lessen it in my eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T17:03:15-08:00","id":382469,"title":"","content":"Golden Rule: Don't like it? Don't use it.<br /> <br /> In this case this specific ST uses it and that's fine, but beyond that it's up to the individual ST to decid whether to use it or not. I don't see the issue here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":3226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","user":"Boneguard","date":". 10-22-2017, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T17:07:38-08:00","id":382492,"title":"","content":"I'm assuming that by &quot;Mystery Play&quot; you mean prelude with Imbuing.<br /> <br /> It is, ultimately, the ST's choice to require you to play out the prelude. However the prelude is not supposed to remove player agency. You and your ST are supposed to work together to craft on that gets you the Creed you selected.<br /> <br /> Lots of people like to do preludes where they don't know what Creed they'll get. But this is not a requirement, or even the default mode, of the game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T17:53:00-08:00","id":382516,"title":"","content":"Just seconding everything Heavy Arms stated above. If you wanted to play an Innocent, the ST shouldn't have changed your creed without agreement from you.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T09:55:03-08:00","id":383250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/382430-mystery-plays-in-hunter-the-reckoning-a-problem#post382430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that the Mystery Play has to happen tells me that I have less creative control over character creation and the fate of my character's awakening is in the hands of the ST, who may have different ideas on which path my character must travel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm afraid that you (and likely your ST as well) are misunderstanding what the book says about preludes.<br /> <br /> The book says that each Hunter has a prelude. It then gives the Storyteller great freedom in how to run that prelude. Your Storyteller chose to run it one way (and I think he chose very poorly), but you can run it very differently.<br /> <br /> For my game, I told my players all about the different Creeds, but didn't let them choose right away. Then I carefully set up a prelude story where they had the opportunity to become any of the (core book) Creeds, and I pointed out how their intended actions might fit one Creed or another. In the end, they still got the Creeds they wanted, and we were all satisfied that those Creeds fit the characters, rather than just being about &quot;cool powers&quot;.<br /> <br /> A few months later, when we added a player, we just let her choose' her Creed outright, and adjusted the story to help her get it. Both methods were equally true to the letter and spirit of the rules.<br /> <br /> Also, just to satisfy my curiosity, would you mind telling us more about what happened in your prelude? Hermit is essentially playing &quot;hard-mode,&quot; and I wouldn't _allow_, let alone _force_ a player to take Hermit unless I thought they could handle it. It sounds like your ST wasn't very experienced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":966,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","user":"Redford_Blade","date":". 01-27-2015, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T10:09:01-08:00","id":383261,"title":"","content":"It would suck to discover that your character essentially shouldn't really interact with the other PCs. <br /> <br /> I started a HtR game where one of the starting &quot;conceits&quot; was what you are describing. The players made up perfectly ordinary people and they were all tossed in a situation where they had to deal with the supernatural. There were several different ways they could approach the situation. Based on the way they had their characters act, I &quot;assigned&quot; a Creed. However, they all KNEW that was how things were going to go and they all agreed to it in advance. Though no one wanted to change their Creed after the fact, I'm pretty sure we would have had a conversation about it and seen how to work things out relative to the story-as-already-told to ret-con in the change. (Also, Waywards and Hermits were officially off the table due to the problems those Creeds can bring to the table in most Hunter groups.)<br /> <br /> I've played in a Vampire game where your Clan was decided by a secret vote of all the players (inlcuding you and the Storyteller). You made yourself up as a mortal and got to role-play through the Embrace. (An aside: It's an interesting experiment to see how your role-playing is coming across to the rest of your group.) I ended up as a Ventrue. That was definitely not the Clan I cast my own vote for. But I ran with it and had an amazing time. Once again, we all signed on for it. <br /> <br /> No one should have to play a character they don't want to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}